    "cost_closing_html":  "About \u003cstrong\u003e${{cost_ps}} a bowl\u003c/strong\u003e (at everyday cost), and the pork chops are nearly the entire bill. The potatoes, carrots and tomatoes that make up the rest of the pot barely register.",
    "shop_smart":  [
                       "\u003cstrong\u003eBuy the family pack of bone-in pork chops.\u003c/strong\u003e Bone-in costs less per pound than boneless and the bones make the sauce taste like it simmered all day.",
                       "\u003cstrong\u003ePotatoes in the big bag are the cheapest calories in the store.\u003c/strong\u003e This pot uses a lot of them, and buying the ten pound bag instead of loose is one of the biggest single savings in the whole recipe.",
                       "\u003cstrong\u003eSazon seasoning is the shortcut Colombian cooks actually use.\u003c/strong\u003e A box of packets costs very little and it delivers the color and savor that would otherwise take a long list of jars.",
                       "\u003cstrong\u003eGreen onions and cilantro are the finish, not the base.\u003c/strong\u003e One bunch of each is plenty. Chop them in at the very end so they stay bright instead of stewing into nothing."
                   ],
    "make_it":  [
                    "Weigh your empty mixing pot and write the number down for portioning later.",
                    "Season the pork chops with salt, black pepper, ground cumin and the sazon seasoning, then brown them in the vegetable oil in a heavy pot, in batches, until both sides have color.",
                    "Cook the diced onion and minced garlic in the same pot until soft, scraping up whatever the pork left behind.",
                    "Add the diced tomatoes with their juice and let them cook down for about five minutes into a thick base.",
                    "Return the pork chops to the pot, tuck in the sliced carrots and the peeled and quartered potatoes, cover tightly, and cook on low heat for about an hour.",
                    "Resist adding water. The vegetables and tomato give off enough liquid to make the sauce, and that is where the flavor concentration comes from.",
                    "When the potatoes are fork tender, stir in the chopped green onions and cilantro and taste for salt."
                ],
